      "summary": "PAD causes leg pain on walking that eases with rest (claudication). NHS: GP assessment, risk-factor control; never invent antiplatelet doses. Emergency (critical ischaemia): sudden cold pale painful limb, rest pain, non-healing ulcers, or black toes — urgent vascular care.",
